      "correspondence": "The canonical isotropic flag has from one to q size steps between λ and 1/2. A small consecutive ratio gives a rational isotropic space. Strong approximation and the real fundamental set express translates in its adelic unipotent radical by a rational element, two real exponentials and a finite congruence element. A probability average of the differences from φ(x) equals φ(x), since the unipotent constant term is zero. Cauchy–Schwarz converts the two real square-sum bounds to a placewise sum.",
