    "The reconstruction uses the rapid-decay theorem for cuspidal forms, the real packet with its integral variation estimate, the canonical isotropic lattice filtration, strong approximation for its unipotent radical and the quantitative real fundamental set. The first depth inequality and its use here are independent of the remaining arithmetic inequalities fitting the chosen congruence ideal to the period."
